OL,4,CBadenoch defends amputee marathon      
OL,5,Crunners claim in benefits cut row      
OL,6,GConservative leader Kemi Badenoch has  
OL,7,Gdefended her suggestion that because   
OL,8,Gdouble amputees run marathons more     
OL,9,Gdisabled people should work instead of 
OL,10,Gclaiming benefits.                     
OL,12,FBadenoch had used the example when     
OL,13,Fsetting out her party's plans to cut   
OL,14,Fwelfare spending by #36bn a year.      
OL,16,FHer comments were criticised by        
OL,17,FParalympian Richard Whitehead, who     
OL,18,Faccused her of "weaponising" his       
OL,19,Fsporting success, while Prime Minister 
OL,20,FAndy Burnham called the Tory leader's  
OL,21,Fwords "crass and insensitive".         
OL,22,                                   G2/4 
